sections.enonce_markdown:
A basket contains $4$ ripe mangoes and $6$ unripe mangoes. Two mangoes are picked at random, one after the other, **without replacement**. Find the probability that:

(a) both are ripe;

(b) one is ripe and one is unripe;

(c) at least one is ripe.

items.enonce_markdown:
A fair coin is tossed and a fair six-sided die is rolled. Find the probability of getting:

(a) a head and a six;

(b) a tail and an odd number;

(c) a head or an even number (or both).
